{"resourceIdentifier":"2722","resourceName":"Inner Mongolia Alongshan Improved Forest Management Project","description":"The Inner Mongolia Alongshan Improved Forest Management Project (hereafter “the project”) is located in northern part of the western side of Greater Khingan Mountains, Hulun Buir City, Inner Mongolia Autonomous Region, P.R.C. It is implemented by Alongshan Forest Industry Co. LTD, China Inner Mongolia Forest Industry Group to protect the once logging forest. \r\n\r\nThe proposed project is implemented in Alongshan, Nannianghe and Talangkong forest farms (hereafter referred to as Alongshan, Nannianghe and Talangkong), which is affiliated to Alongshan Forest Bureau. The project has approximately 69,517 ha commercial forest with 25,784, 31,515and 12,218 ha in Alongshan, Nannianghe and Talangkong forest farm respectively. The forest ages range from sapling, middle age to mature forest. Prior to the implementation of the project, the forest within the project area was designed and planted as commercial forest, and logged annually according to the timber production plan issued by Alongshan Forest Bureau. Since the project started in 2016, the commercial harvest has been cancelled and only tending and managing is allowed.\r\n\r\nThe project is expected to generate approximately 9,732,223 tCO2e during the 30 years’ crediting period, with the annual emission reductions of 324,407 tCO2e.\r\n\r\n The project activity will significantly improve the forest management conditions within the project area, and benefit local ecological environment. The implementation of the project will not only achieve a reliable measurable carbon sequestration by reducing commercial timer, but also contribute to sustainable development of the local community.","location":{"latitude":51.739760,"longitude":121.636800},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-04-13","endExclusive":"2022-05-14","endInclusive":"2022-05-13"},"attributes":[{"code":